item.text:
Accepted new evidence only for the 1B gaps.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin to oversee military drills as tensions mount over Ukraine","publisher":"Euronews with AP","publication_date":"2022-02-18","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/02/18/putin-to-oversee-military-drills-as-tensions-mount-over-ukraine","claim":"Russia announced massive drills of its nuclear forces on February 18, 2022, and said Vladimir Putin would supervise exercises of the strategic forces with the firing of ballistic and cruise missiles to test readiness and reliability.","locator":"lines 656-665","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous AP-based reporting with a direct ministry statement; secondary but specific and date-stamped.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period, February 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High: the exercise was announced as under Putin's supervision, so the command choice is attributable to him through his supreme-command role; the operational detail comes from the defence ministry.","contrary_evidence":["Putin and Kremlin officials publicly denied plans to invade Ukraine"],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.8","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia Freezes U.S. Inspections Of Its Nuclear Arsenal Under New START","publisher":"RFE/RL","publication_date":"2022-08-09","url":"https://www.rferl.org/a/russia-freezes-us-inspections-nuclear-arsenal-start/31979803.html","claim":"Russia informed the United States that it was freezing U.S. inspections under New START, said the move was temporary, and claimed it remained fully committed to the treaty's provisions.","locator":"lines 124-135","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report quoting the Russian Foreign Ministry statement; strong for the fact of the policy change, weaker for Putin-personal intent.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period, August 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the action was taken by the Russian Foreign Ministry under Putin's presidency; the source does not show a personal signature, but it is Russia's nuclear-arms-control posture under his authority.","contrary_evidence":["The Russian statement framed the freeze as temporary and treaty-consistent, which is a self-justifying claim rather than independent verification."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.4","1B.8","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"U.S. Conditions Talks on New START Inspections","publisher":"Arms Control Association","publication_date":"2022-10","url":"https://www.armscontrol.org/act/2022-10/news/us-conditions-talks-new-start-inspections","claim":"The U.S. said any follow-on nuclear arms-control talks depended on resuming New START inspections, while Russia had impeded those inspections and further extended the pause by prohibiting inspections of relevant facilities in August 2022.","locator":"lines 80-86","source_type":"ngo","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialist arms-control reporting summarizing official U.S. and Russian positions; useful for treaty mechanics and the attribution of the inspection freeze.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period, October 2022, summarizing August 2022 action.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the inspection impasse is attributable to Russia's state decision under Putin's authority, though the article also records Russia's sanctions/visa explanation.","contrary_evidence":["U.S. officials said sanctions did not prevent Russian inspections, so Russia's justification was disputed."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.8","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia notifies U.S. it will carry out expected nuclear drills","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-10-26","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/russia-notifies-us-it-will-carry-out-expected-nuclear-drills-2922923","claim":"Russia notified the United States about annual strategic nuclear-force exercises, and U.S. officials said that this notification lowered the risk of miscalculation under the New START framework.","locator":"lines 422-436","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting with direct U.S. and Russian official quotations; strong for the notification and risk-reduction effect.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period, October 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High: the drills were a Russian state action under Putin's command authority and were presented as routine annual exercises with advance notification.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes Putin's earlier nuclear threats and the dirty-bomb allegation, which cut against a clean risk-reduction reading."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.4","1B.8","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia asserts control over Ukraine nuclear plant, Kyiv disagrees","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-10-05","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/putin-asserts-control-over-ukraine-nuclear-plant-kyiv-disagrees-2905308","claim":"Putin ordered the Russian government to take control of the Zaporizhzhia nuclear power plant, while the U.N. nuclear watchdog warned that the plant's power supply was extremely fragile.","locator":"lines 403-409","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting on a specific Putin order and the nuclear-safety warning from the IAEA.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period, October 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High: the order is directly attributed to Putin; the plant-control move and the ensuing safety risk are ruler-level decisions in his sphere of authority.","contrary_evidence":["Ukraine and international observers disputed Russia's legal authority over the plant."],"lenses":["1B.5","1B.8","1B.9","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia Claims to Federalize Ukrainian Nuclear Plant","publisher":"Arms Control Association","publication_date":"2022-11","url":"https://www.armscontrol.org/act/2022-11/news/russia-claims-federalize-ukrainian-nuclear-plant","claim":"After Putin announced federalization of Zaporizhzhia, Russia said the plant should be operated under the supervision of its agencies, while the IAEA reported continued pressure on Ukrainian plant staff and a serious impact on safety decision-making after the kidnapping of the Ukrainian plant head.","locator":"lines 85-95","source_type":"ngo","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialist nuclear-arms-control reporting that combines IAEA and Russian statements; strong on the safety consequences of the occupation and federalization move.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period, October-November 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High for the federalization order and occupation posture; the pressure on staff and safety interference are attributable to the Russian-controlled environment under Putin's authority.","contrary_evidence":["Russia claimed the move was designed to ensure safe operation, but that was disputed by Ukraine and the IAEA context in the same report."],"lenses":["1B.5","1B.8","1B.9","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Attacks on Ukrainian Nuclear Plant Intensify","publisher":"Arms Control Association","publication_date":"2022-09","url":"https://www.armscontrol.org/act/2022-09/news/attacks-ukrainian-nuclear-plant-intensify","claim":"Russia occupied Zaporizhzhia at the start of the war, refused to withdraw, and used the operating nuclear facility for stationing troops and munitions, intensifying the nuclear-safety risk.","locator":"lines 80-85","source_type":"ngo","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialist secondary source summarizing the occupation and militarization of the plant; strong for the mechanism even though it is not the underlying primary filing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period, August-September 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High: the occupation and militarization are attributable to Russian forces acting under Putin's wartime authority.","contrary_evidence":["Russia denied responsibility for some attacks and blamed Ukraine instead."],"lenses":["1B.5","1B.8","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia is playing roulette with nuclear safety: UK statement at UN Security Council","publisher":"GOV.UK","publication_date":"2022-09-06","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/russia-is-playing-roulette-with-nuclear-safety-uk-statement-at-un-security-council","claim":"The UK told the Security Council that IAEA had confirmed Russian military personnel, vehicles, and equipment at Zaporizhzhia, that the plant's physical integrity had been violated several times, and that Russia's occupation was making safe operation impossible.","locator":"lines 95-113","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official transcript of a Security Council statement quoting the IAEA-backed findings; indirect for the fact pattern but strong and date-specific.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period, September 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate to high: it concerns Russian military occupation and the resulting risk posture under Putin's control, though the quoted statement is from the UK rather than Russia.","contrary_evidence":["Russia disputes the characterization and framed the situation as Ukraine's fault."],"lenses":["1B.5","1B.8","1B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Путин заявил, что ядерная угроза нарастает, но РФ не применит ядерное оружие первой","publisher":"Интерфакс","publication_date":"2022-12-07","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/russia/875831","claim":"Putin said the nuclear threat was growing but Russia would not be the first to use nuclear weapons, describing nuclear arms as defensive and saying Russia would respond only to a strike against its territory.","locator":"lines 34-46","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous transcript-style reporting with Putin quotations; strong primary-style evidence for his stated doctrine and rhetoric.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period, December 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High: the statements are directly Putin's, made in an official setting.","contrary_evidence":["The same year included repeated Russian nuclear threats and coercive nuclear signaling toward Ukraine and the West."],"lenses":["1B.2","1B.3","1B.8","1B.10"]}

Search ledger, follow-up wave only, approximate:
- candidates found: about 35 distinct candidate pages/records
- direct opens: 9
- find-based line extractions: 6
- duplicates/near-duplicates dropped: about 15
- irrelevant or out-of-period: about 4
- inaccessible or timeout/paywall failures: about 6
- accepted distinct URLs: 8

Gap status:
- Direct 2022 command-and-control discipline and nuclear exercise behavior: partly resolved.
- Treaty / inspection / nonproliferation mechanics: resolved for this wave.
- Zaporizhzhia nuclear-safety posture and coercive shielding of conventional war: resolved enough to support the dossier.
- Expert appointments and risk-reducing nuclear-security staffing: not recoverable in this round.
- Direct ruler-level evidence on dual-use catastrophic-risk policy beyond nuclear: not recoverable in this round.
- End-of-period posture: partly resolved, but still net more dangerous than inherited.

Blockers:
- Several kremlin.ru and IAEA pages timed out or required access that the browser could not complete.
- I did not find a clean 2022 Putin-specific appointment record that clearly adds new nuclear safety expertise beyond the already visible command structure.
- I did not find credible Putin-specific 2022 evidence for bio/cyber/AI catastrophic-risk management worth retaining here.
